=520  \\$aJAKE is a free website developed at Yale Medical Library that allows you to search for a journal to see which databases index it and/or include the full-text. You can search by journal title; database title; ISSN; or citation to a specific article using journal title, volumes, issue, page and year. This site is unique in giving us a way to keep current on the constantly changing nature of serials in electronic format. There are roughly 23,000 journals included in 200 databases, and many are full-text.$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
