=520  \\$a“…this very thorough website was created to complement a major television series on the history of the Supreme Court that will soon appear on PBS. Within each one of the site’s sections, users will find essays and teaching materials on gender equality, social rights, personal liberties, and equal access to schools. The site also includes a very nice interactive timeline of landmark cases handed down since 1792. Finally, the site also includes a searchable encyclopedia of terms and court cases of note.”$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
