=520  \\$aThis site is a collaboration between Street Law and The Supreme Court Historical Society, and was developed to provide teachers with a full range of resources and activities to support the teaching of landmark Supreme Court cases. While these activities are online, many of them can be adapted for use in a one-computer classroom or a classroom with no computer. The general teaching strategies include moot court, political cartoon analysis, continuum exercises, and Web site evaluation.$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
