=520  \\$aCivil War Washington examines the U.S. national capital from multiple perspectives as a case study of social, political, cultural, and medical/scientific transitions provoked or accelerated by the Civil War. The project draws on the methods of many fields–literary studies, history, geography, computer-aided mapping–to create a digital resource that chronicles the war’s impact on the city.$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
