=520  \\$aThe online Repository of Historical Gun Laws was created by the faculty of the Center for Firearms Law at Duke Law School. “A searchable free database of gun laws from the Middle Ages to 1776 in England and from the Colonial Era to the middle of the twentieth century in the United States. This repository is intended as a resource for scholars and practitioners interested in historical laws concerning firearms and other similar weapons.”$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
