=520  \\$aThe mission of United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) is to protect human health and the environment and to ensure that Americans have clean air, land and water, as well as to promote national efforts to reduce environmental risks are based on the best available scientific information. All parts of society–communities, individuals, businesses, and state, local and tribal governments–have access to accurate information sufficient to effectively participate in managing human health and environmental risks. Contaminated lands and toxic sites are cleaned up by potentially responsible parties and revitalized. Chemicals in the marketplace are also reviewed for safety.$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
