=520  \\$aPACER (acronym) for Public Access to Court Electronic Records) is an electronic public access service of United States federal court documents. It allows users to obtain case and docket information from the United States district courts, United States courts of appeals, and United States courts of bankruptcy court. It holds more than 500 million documents.$cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month
